content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-113 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22650",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Reported drive-end vibration is 4.8 mm/s. The applicable HF-300 criterion is Figure 3, using vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. This value is provisionally Zone C because it is strictly between 4.5 and 7.1 mm/s RMS: “Restricted — plan maintenance.” It is not in Zone D and does not itself trigger the highest-zone immediate-stop rule. Overall pump classification still requires the highest reading from both bearing housings.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For the reported housing temperature of 70 C, the applicable criterion is bearing-housing surface temperature. Normal is up to 70 C, alarm is 80 C, and trip is 90 C; therefore 70 C is at the upper limit of normal, below alarm and trip. It does not meet the site requirement for a priority-1 work order, which applies when temperature is above the manufacturer's alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leakage is reported, and no numerical allowable-leakage limit is supplied. The report therefore does not present the manual's “leakage at shaft seal” symptom or, on that observation alone, indicate mechanical-seal replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "First check shaft misalignment: it is a documented probable cause of high vibration, and the vibration began after motor replacement. Laser alignment is required after work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear is the next documented possibility to investigate. Replace both bearings as a pair only if either shows wear, noise or high temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage is another documented cause of high vibration; inspect the impeller before selecting replacement work.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation is also a documented cause; check NPSH as part of the high-vibration diagnosis.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Verify the reported drive-end measurement and measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings. Record the results in mm/s RMS and classify the highest reading using Figure 3 before intrusive work.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check and, where necessary, correct shaft alignment using a laser alignment tool following the motor work. The applicable tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular offset 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For the high-vibration symptom, inspect the bearings and impeller and check NPSH. Record any bearing wear or noise, impeller imbalance or damage, and evidence relevant to cavitation; do not condemn components without inspection findings.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Where listed pump fasteners are disturbed during inspection or repair, reassemble with lightly oiled threads and tighten to Table 5: M16 casing bolts 210 Nm; M24 impeller nut 160 Nm; M10 seal gland nuts 25 Nm; M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After alignment and any resulting repair, repeat vibration measurements on both bearing housings, classify the highest value using Figure 3, and recheck housing surface temperature against the 70 C normal, 80 C alarm and 90 C trip criteria. Record the final readings before closing the work order.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For any work inside the pump or on its seal, apply electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit after draining and venting.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the back pull-out assembly is lifted, its documented mass is 68 kg, exceeding the 25 kg threshold. Use a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the lines are chemically dosed, wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If vibration is classified in Zone D, the manufacturer's highest severity zone, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. Figure 3 labels Zone D “Damage likely — stop the pump.”",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If bearing-housing temperature rises above the manufacturer's 80 C alarm limit, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift; the documented trip temperature is 90 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain the documented Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Planned laser alignment allowance: 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional allowance only if bearing replacement is justified by inspection: bearing-pair replacement is 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [],
  "open_questions": [
    "Is the reported 4.8 mm/s value an RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing, and what is the non-drive-end bearing-housing reading? Only the drive-end value is reported.",
    "Did the motor replacement move the motor or bearing housing, and was post-replacement laser alignment performed? Provide the measured parallel and angular offsets if available.",
    "What are the bearing inspection findings, impeller condition and NPSH/cavitation findings? No diagnostic results or NPSH acceptance criterion are supplied.",
    "If inspection identifies replacement work, what are the correct bearing, impeller, seal or gasket part numbers and required quantities? The evidence specifies replacing both bearings as a pair but provides no part numbers.",
    "Are the pump lines chemically dosed, so that the conditional chemical goggles and nitrile-glove control applies?",
    "No standard labour times are supplied for vibration verification, bearing and impeller inspection, NPSH checking or post-work testing; the final schedule requires those durations."
  ]
}
